## Purpose

Turn dashboard warning counts into an explainable daily-review surface. Derive controlled
attention conditions and recent changes from already accepted, privacy-bounded reports while local
Tool Shed state remains authoritative and the hosted service remains advisory and read-only.

## Desired Outcome

An operator can see why a project or instance needs attention, when the condition began or became
stale, its affected source, and a safe local Tool Shed investigation route. A combined recent feed
shows lifecycle and controlled operational changes once, highlights entries since the browser's
last visit, and never converts repeated reports or heartbeats into history.

## First Useful Boundary

- Derive a stable controlled attention registry from blocked work, unreconciled outcomes,
  reporter/App Server failures, and stale instances.
- Keep active and resolved attention distinct; unresolved conditions cannot be acknowledged away.
- Render fleet-level and project-level attention with severity, source, age/freshness, detail
  links, and server-owned local investigation guidance.
- Combine existing lifecycle and material events into a bounded, change-only recent feed.
- Store the last-visit marker only in browser local storage and use it solely for presentation.
- Reuse semantic SSE refresh and the existing 90-day event retention.
- Implement and deploy the complete slice through Work2; formal release remains a later Work5 gate.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Attention truth | Stable controlled reasons, deterministic activation/clearing, timestamps, severity, and safe route mapping | current report state and freshness |
| Recent changes | One normalized lifecycle/material/attention feed with stable change identity and browser-local visit highlighting | existing change-only event stores |
| Dashboard experience | Fleet and project attention cards, useful links, source/freshness context, and accessible new-change treatment | attention and recent-change projections |
| Qualification | Focused derivation, ingestion, rendering, privacy, SSE, migration, deployment, and browser evidence | complete vertical slice |

## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G1-ATTENTION-CONTRACT` requires bounded reason, severity, source, freshness, deduplication, and
   deterministic clearing without arbitrary reporter text.
2. `G2-RECENT-CHANGE-SEMANTICS` requires a change-only recent feed and a privacy-safe visit boundary
   that never acknowledges or hides unresolved attention.
3. `G3-ACTIONABLE-ADVISORY-UI` requires controlled reasons, affected sources, age/freshness, hosted
   detail links, and safe local investigation routes while preserving read-only advisory hosting.

## Constraints

- Use controlled server-owned labels and routes only; never render reporter-supplied arbitrary text.
- Preserve per-instance freshness and do not let one current instance hide another stale source.
- Do not add server-side page-view tracking, remote acknowledgement, or remote command execution.
- Reuse the existing material/lifecycle stores and bounded retention rather than creating a second
  telemetry or notification system.
- Keep public documentation routes and dashboard authentication compatible.

## Non-Goals

- Email, paging, webhooks, or outbound notification delivery.
- Remote mitigation, acknowledgement that hides unresolved state, or lifecycle mutation.
- Raw logs, paths, commands, diagnostics, credentials, or free-form summaries.
- Historical reconstruction before controlled events existed.

